    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d64">

                <pb facs="0185" n="115" sameAs="frus:frus1919Parisv01/pg115"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">033.1140/246: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Special Representative</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >House</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Paris</hi>
                        </placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1918-10-30T21:00:00+00:00"
                            >October 30, 1918—9 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received October 31—6:15 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>22. For Polk from Auchincloss. Colonel House wishes Mezes to be asked to send him
                    a cable advising him of the progress and difficulties of “Inquiry” since his
                    departure. He wishes further to be fully advised regarding this work by
                    cable.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Edward House</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
